	Wall Street Blues, adopted from a board game, is a much better
program than most stock market games. You may spend a total of two minutes
a day inside this game, which is about the amount of time you may spend on
the phone with your broker. The prices are updated during nightly
maintenance, which is also the time the high scores and rankings are
computed. When stock prices pass $200 per share the stock splits giving
everyone twice as many shares as they had before and the price per share
drops to $108. If a stock drops below $1 per share then that share goes
bankrupt and everyone loses the number of shares of that stock that they
owned. The stock price then stays at $0 for the entire day and will not
allow anyone to purchase any of that stock. During maintenance that night
the stock is reinitialized to $100 per share and then under goes the normal
price changes. That stock can then be purchased again. Resets are done on
the first of every month. Reset will take the current game and save it to 
last months winners.  This game was designed not to run longer than 31 days. 
Every day in this game is represented as being one year.
