	4 December 1994: v2.0 Well, finally an update! What to improve on
this fine game? Well, I started by expanding the company biographies
(Renamed to Company Prospectus). Seems you always have one of these before
you get into any investing anyway. It now gives you a history of the stocks
performance and an average gain percentage. Any of your users try to keep
this on paper? I also added the menu items for the screens you see when you
first get into the game. Seems I was always getting out of the game and
going back in to see them again. I added the Dow Jones index and the Dow
Jones percentage of gain. This works like a users account owning 1 share of
each stock. When splits occur then it adds a share so the index keeps
rising. When a stock goes bankrupt then it resets the shares in the Dow
Jones to 1. I haven't heard from anybody on suggestions for changes so the
resulting product is from my own imagination from the basic game. I do
appreciate the few people who have called to inform me of the bugs they
found. It helps alot in getting out a quality game.

INSTALATION:  THIS VERSION WILL NOT WORK WITH EARLIER VERSIONS!

	1. Uncrunch the LHA archive into your Pfiles/Stocks directory. Adopt
WallStreet into your pfiles as an AREXX program.
	2. Add Date to your BBS Events to run every day. (also AREXX)
What time you have it run really doesn't matter.
	3. If you want to reward your wealthiest player then add TimeAward
to your sys.welcome file. When a caller calls the first time of the day he 
will be given 30 minutes of extra time online. This time disappears if not 
used during the first call of the day. In your sys.welcome file the line 
should read;

      {#0Pfiles/Stocks/TimeAward}
      ^ 
      | This is a control Q

NOTE: All files should be in pfiles/stocks directory!


UPDATING FROM EARLIER VERSIONS;
 You must copy all new files over the old files! The new files have been
changed so much that they will not work with earlier version files. The
following files which relate to the running of your current game do not
have to be changed or deleted;

ST.DATA
U3
U4
SU.DATA
T3
Winning

 As long as these files stay intact, you can update and continue your
current game. One exception is that earlier version allowed only $10,000 to
start with and the current version allows $20,000. You can edit the
individual data files to give them an additional $10,000 if you like. That
figure should be stored on the second to the last line.

